# Elevator Motion Problems

**Given:**
- Building height: 40 floors × 5 m = **200 m**
- Acceleration/deceleration: $a = 1 \, \text{m/s}^2$
- Maximum speed: $v_{max} = 5 \, \text{m/s}$
- Ground floor (1/F) is at height $h = 0$
- Top floor (40/F) is at height $h = 39 \times 5 = 195 \, \text{m}$

*(Note: Floor numbering — 1/F is ground at 0 m, 2/F is at 5 m, ..., 40/F is at 39×5 = 195 m.)*

---

## Question 1: Time to go from 1/F to 40/F

**Distance:** $d = 195 \, \text{m}$

The elevator accelerates at $1 \, \text{m/s}^2$ until reaching max speed, then cruises, then decelerates at $1 \, \text{m/s}^2$.

**Acceleration phase:**
- Time to reach max speed: $t_1 = \frac{v_{max}}{a} = \frac{5}{1} = 5 \, \text{s}$
- Distance covered during acceleration: $d_1 = \frac{1}{2} a t_1^2 = \frac{1}{2} \times 1 \times 25 = 12.5 \, \text{m}$

**Deceleration phase:**
- Time to stop: $t_3 = \frac{v_{max}}{a} = 5 \, \text{s}$
- Distance during deceleration: $d_3 = 12.5 \, \text{m}$

**Cruising phase:**
- Distance: $d_2 = d - d_1 - d_3 = 195 - 12.5 - 12.5 = 170 \, \text{m}$
- Time: $t_2 = \frac{d_2}{v_{max}} = \frac{170}{5} = 34 \, \text{s}$

**Total time:**
$$t = t_1 + t_2 + t_3 = 5 + 34 + 5 = \boxed{44 \, \text{s}}$$

---

## Question 2: Two people, one to 10/F and one to 30/F

**Person 1 → 10/F:** height = $9 \times 5 = 45 \, \text{m}$
**Person 2 → 30/F:** height = $29 \times 5 = 145 \, \text{m}$

The lift goes up to 10/F first (drop off person 1), then continues to 30/F (drop off person 2).

**Leg 1: 0 → 45 m**
- Accelerate: 5 s, 12.5 m
- Cruise: $45 - 12.5 = 32.5 \, \text{m}$ → $t = 32.5/5 = 6.5 \, \text{s}$
- Decelerate: 5 s, 12.5 m
- Total leg 1: $5 + 6.5 + 5 = 16.5 \, \text{s}$

**Leg 2: 45 → 145 m** (distance = 100 m)
- Accelerate: 5 s, 12.5 m
- Cruise: $100 - 12.5 - 12.5 = 75 \, \text{m}$ → $t = 75/5 = 15 \, \text{s}$
- Decelerate: 5 s, 12.5 m
- Total leg 2: $5 + 15 + 5 = 25 \, \text{s}$

**Total time:**
$$16.5 + 25 = \boxed{41.5 \, \text{s}}$$

---

